# See https://docs.github.com/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files for more about ignoring files.

# Compiled output
/dist
/tmp
/out-tsc
/bazel-out

# Staging directory for the E2E client image. .github/workflows/e2e-client-image.yml assembles the
# docker build context here (built output + docker/e2e/nginx.conf and nothing else) so that no
# source can enter the context in the first place.
/.image-context

# Staging directory for the public web client image, assembled the same way by
# .github/workflows/web-client-image.yml (built output + docker/web/*.conf and nothing else).
/.web-context

# wasm-pack output for the browser build, produced by `bun run build:wasm`.
#
# A build artifact, not a source file, and deliberately not committed: it is the compiled form of
# crates/venta-crypto, so a committed copy is a second place for the crypto engine to exist and the
# only one anybody would notice going stale. CI builds it before `ng build` in both ci.yml's
# frontend job and web-client-image.yml, and both assert the blob is present afterwards - `ng
# build` copies src/assets with a `**/*` glob and a glob that matches nothing is not an error, so
# a missing engine is otherwise silent.
/src/assets/wasm/

# Node
/node_modules
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# IDEs and editors
.idea/
.project
.classpath
.c9/
*.launch
.settings/
*.sublime-workspace

.zed/

# Visual Studio Code
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.history/*

# Miscellaneous
/.angular/cache
.sass-cache/
/connect.lock
/coverage
/libpeerconnection.log
testem.log
/typings

# System files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Sentry Config File
.sentryclirc

# Superpowers subagent-driven-development scratch workspace
.superpowers/

# The SADIE II measurements the bundled HRIR sphere is built from.
#
# A 112 MB build input, not a source file: the sphere it produces
# (src-tauri/assets/hrir/sadie_d1_48k.bin) is what ships, and it is committed. GitHub rejects any
# push carrying a file this large, so an accidental `git add -A` here blocks the whole branch
# rather than just adding weight. src-tauri/assets/hrir/NOTICE.md has the Zenodo record to fetch it
# from and the command to regenerate the sphere.
D1.zip

# Transcripts from scripts/run-release.mjs. One file per run of the release build; useful to
# attach to a bug report, never useful to commit.
/logs

# Cargo output at the repository root.
#
# New with the workspace: `src-tauri/.gitignore` has covered `/target/` since there was only one
# crate, and that rule is scoped to that directory. A workspace puts `target/` beside its *root*
# manifest, and `.cargo/config.toml` pins `target-dir` back to `src-tauri/target` for the sake of
# build.yml's upload globs - but any cargo invocation that runs before or outside that config still
# lands here, and this directory reached 6.3 GB unignored. Same trap the D1.zip note above describes,
# two orders of magnitude larger.
/target

# Per-machine Claude Code state. settings.local.json is a permission allowlist built up by
# whoever is sitting at the machine, so it conflicts on every pull and means nothing to anyone
# else. It was tracked until now; see the history rewrite that removed it.
.claude